---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, social } from '../data/site';
const jsonLd = [
  { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'ProfilePage', mainEntity: { '@id': `${site.url}/#person` }, url: `${site.url}/about/`, name: `About ${site.author.name}` },
  { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'BreadcrumbList', itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: site.url + '/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'About', item: site.url + '/about/' } ] },
];
---
<Base title="About" description="Edison Bujupi is a cybersecurity engineer and Wazuh Ambassador who documents detection engineering and security monitoring experiments from his own lab." path="/about/" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <div class="wrap page article-page">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <span aria-current="page">About</span></nav>
    <h1>About</h1>
    <div class="article-grid"><div class="prose">
      <p>I am {site.author.name}, a cybersecurity engineer. I document what I test in my own lab and keep experience, research and experiments clearly separate.</p>
      <p>This website is where I publish those technical notes: how security events are produced, how they become alerts, and what has to be true before an alert is worth reading.</p>
      <h2>Focus</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Detection engineering and Wazuh rules</li>
        <li>Security monitoring and incident investigation</li>
        <li>Linux audit logging and Windows event analysis</li>
        <li>Network security, infrastructure and documented experiments</li>
      </ul>
      <p>These are the areas I work on and write about. They are not a list of finished projects: the <a href="/research/">research</a> and <a href="/projects/">projects</a> pages show what exists.</p>
      <h2>How I separate the work</h2>
      <p>I keep four kinds of work apart, because they carry different weight.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Independent research and lab experiments.</strong> Work I do in my own environment, with the configuration, the commands and the results published.</li>
        <li><strong>Demonstrations and proofs of concept.</strong> Short demonstrations that show one idea. They are labelled as demonstrations.</li>
        <li><strong>Community contributions.</strong> Work I contribute to the Wazuh Ambassadors Program. My approved contributions are listed on the <a href="/wazuh-ambassador/">Wazuh Ambassador page</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Professional experience.</strong> Listed only when I can state it precisely.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Wazuh Ambassador</h2>
      <p>I am a member of the Wazuh Ambassadors Program. My approved contributions are listed on the <a href="/wazuh-ambassador/">Wazuh Ambassador page</a>. This website is independent and is not operated or endorsed by Wazuh.</p>
      {(social.github || social.linkedin) && (
        <>
          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>
            {social.github && <>The best place to reach me is <a href={social.github} rel="me noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">GitHub</a>.</>}
            {social.linkedin && <> You can also find me on <a href={social.linkedin} rel="me noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>.</>}
          </p>
        </>
      )}
    </div></div>
  </div>
</Base>
